MailDigest — self-hosted mirror mailbox on {{domain}}

Mail address of the mailbox: {{address}}
IMAP host / port:            {{domain}} / 993 (IMAPS)
IMAP username:               {{address}}
Certificate directory:       {{cert_dir}}

Five steps. Everything privileged happens below with your own sudo; MailDigest itself
neither installs nor changes anything on this system.

{{steps}}

What this mailbox is, and what it is not:

  * It accepts exactly one recipient: {{address}}. Mail to any other address at
    {{domain}} is refused at RCPT TO, so there is no backscatter and no mailbox for
    root@{{domain}}. There is deliberately no postmaster@ and no abuse@ mailbox either,
    although RFC 5321 expects one from a host that receives mail: this host is a private
    sink for one person's forwarded mail. If your provider or your own policy insists on
    a postmaster address, add it by hand to virtual_mailbox_maps in postfix.sh and apply
    it again.
  * The random local part is the spam defence — nobody guesses {{address}}. Rotate it by
    deleting this directory and running `maildigest selfhost-mail --domain {{domain}}`
    again; the old address stops working as soon as you apply the new files.
  * Port 25 has to be reachable from the internet. Home connections almost never are:
    inbound 25 is blocked and the address changes. From another machine:
      openssl s_client -starttls smtp -connect {{domain}}:25
  * Inbound TLS is opportunistic on purpose (smtpd_tls_security_level = may). Forwarders
    that cannot negotiate would otherwise give up silently.
  * Certificate renewal is certbot's job. apply.sh installs a deploy hook that reloads
    both services; `maildigest selfhost-mail --check` warns below 14 days left.
  * Nothing in this directory is a secret. apply.sh asks for the mailbox password and
    stores only its BLF-CRYPT hash in /etc/dovecot/users, readable by root and Dovecot
    and nobody else; MailDigest never writes the password anywhere.
  * Supported: Debian 13 and newer, Fedora 43 and newer (Dovecot 2.4 syntax). On Ubuntu
    24.04 the commented 2.3 lines in dovecot.conf apply, and nothing there is verified.
